{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The words of Lemuel, king of Massa, whom his mother chastised</b> — At the beginning of the book he informed that his father chastised him concerning wisdom, and here he recounts that his mother chastised him — Bathsheba — after his father's death, to teach him wisdom: to keep away from women and from wine, for they are the cause of evil and transgression. And on account of their wisdom and their glory, he praised the wise woman in alphabetic order, to serve as a remembrance." "<b>Lemuel</b> — he is Solomon. And it is possible that he was so called because in his days they had one El and did not serve idols; likewise the one who stands on His throne is called with us El."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:46.735143391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}